        "problem": "Simplify the expression $[(P\u21d2\u00acQ)\u2227P]\u2227Q.$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operation\n\n- First, we use the associative law:\n\n$$\n[(P\u21d2\u00acQ)\u2227P]\u2227Q\u2261(P\u21d2\u00acQ)\u2227(P\u2227Q)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use that $X\u21d2Y\u2261\u00acX\u2228Y:$\n\n$$\n(P\u21d2\u00acQ)\u2227(P\u2227Q)\u2261(\u00acP\u2228\u00acQ)\u2227(P\u2227Q)\n$$\n\n- Next, we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n(\u00acP\u2228\u00acQ)\u2227(P\u2227Q)\u2261\u00ac(P\u2227Q)\u2227(P\u2227Q)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n\u00ac(P\u2227Q)\u2227(P\u2227Q)\u2261c\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n[(P\u21d2\u00acQ)\u2227P]\u2227Q\u2261c.\n$$",
